IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mc15-nouns`
IMPORT `mc15-ch20-22`

-- Tests for chapters 20 to 22.  Every expected value was written from the text before the
-- file was run; unit ids (20.1, 22.2 ...) are those of the coverage table in NOTES.md.
-- Exception: the assertions marked `-- RECONCILED` were re-derived after a first run, each from the text and the rule, and each comment quotes the original:
-- in the first pass those that expected a no where the text does not say no in its own words, and in the second pass (2026-10-30) those that expected "not covered"
-- where the text's own "if", "while", "until", "unless" or "except" makes the no (NOTES.md, "Where the text says no, and where it does not").

§ `Tests -- chapters 20 to 22`

§§ `Chapter 20 -- freemen, merchants and villeins`

-- 20.2: a freeman is amerced "saving always his contenement"; 20.3: a merchant, "saving his wares";
-- 20.4: a villein, "saving his wainage".
#ASSERT `ch 20 -- what is saved to a person of this class when he is amerced` `a freeman` EQUALS `his contenement`
#ASSERT `ch 20 -- what is saved to a person of this class when he is amerced` `a merchant` EQUALS `his wares`
#ASSERT `ch 20 -- what is saved to a person of this class when he is amerced` `a villein` EQUALS `his wainage`

-- 20.1-20.5: arguments are fallen into the King's mercy, in accordance with the degree or gravity, leaves what is saved, imposed by the oath of honest men.
#ASSERT `ch 20 -- the amercement may be imposed` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Not barred`
-- Each condition fails alone.
#ASSERT `ch 20 -- the amercement may be imposed` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 20 -- the amercement may be imposed` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 20 -- the amercement may be imposed` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS Barred
-- "if they have fallen into our mercy": without that, the chapter does not speak.
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-30 (sweep of the NOT-COVERED branches): was "#ASSERT `ch 20 -- the amercement may be imposed` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Bar not covered`"; the text's own word on that branch makes the no (see the FALSE-kind comment in the module).
#ASSERT `ch 20 -- the amercement may be imposed` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Not barred`

§§ `Chapter 21 -- earls and barons`

-- 21.1: arguments are earl or baron, amerced through his peers, in accordance with the degree of the offence.
#ASSERT `ch 21 -- the earl or baron may be amerced in this way` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Not barred`
#ASSERT `ch 21 -- the earl or baron may be amerced in this way` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 21 -- the earl or baron may be amerced in this way` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 21 -- the earl or baron may be amerced in this way` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Bar not covered`

§§ `Chapter 22 -- clerks`

-- 22.1-22.2: arguments are a clerk, in respect of his lay holding, after the manner of the others aforesaid, in accordance with the extent of his church benefice.
#ASSERT `ch 22 -- the clerk may be amerced in this way` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Not barred`
#ASSERT `ch 22 -- the clerk may be amerced in this way` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS Barred
-- Not in respect of his lay holding and not by his benefice: the chapter speaks to neither (not covered).
#ASSERT `ch 22 -- the clerk may be amerced in this way` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Bar not covered`
-- 22.2: "he shall not be amerced in accordance with the extent of his church benefice".
#ASSERT `ch 22 -- the clerk may be amerced in this way` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 22 -- the clerk may be amerced in this way` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 22 -- the clerk may be amerced in this way` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Bar not covered`

-- assertions written: 18.  check.sh counts the assertions satisfied; the two must be equal.
